{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "Here is a 300+ word summary of the Wikipedia page \"Raymond III Count of Tripoli\" without commas and with 3 highlighted sections in markdown format:\n\nRaymond III was Count of Tripoli from 1142 until his death in 1180 he was a member of the House of Fulk and a cousin of King Fulk of Jerusalem \nHe was a prominent figure in the Kingdom of Jerusalem and played a key role in the events leading up to the Battle of Hattin \nRaymond III was born around 1142 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Helena of Armenia\n\n*Raymond III was known for his attempts to strengthen the County of Tripoli through strategic marriages and military campaigns he sought to expand his territories and secure his borders from the growing threat of the Ayyubid dynasty*\n\nRaymond III married Princess Maria of Armenia but the marriage was childless and ended in divorce he later married Agnes of Courtenay but this marriage was also childless \nIn 1177 Raymond III was appointed regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem for the young King Henry I of Jerusalem \nHe played a crucial role in the politics of the kingdom and was a strong opponent of the King's mother Agnes of Courtenay \n\n*The Siege of Acre in 1180 was a significant event during Raymond III's rule he successfully defended the city against an attack by the Ayyubid forces led by Saladin*\nRaymond III died on September 2 1180 without an heir his death led to a succession crisis in the County of Tripoli \nHe was succeeded by his nephew William of Torrès \n\n*Raymond III's legacy is marked by his efforts to maintain the independence of the County of Tripoli in the face of overwhelming pressure from the Ayyubid dynasty his military campaigns and strategic alliances helped to secure the county for several years after his death* \nRaymond III's life and rule are well documented in the writings of medieval historians such as Wil